%% Sequence: a resident asks a question about a decision.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor R as Resident (browser)
  participant S as Server (node:http)
  participant U as Limits + usage
  participant L as Lead agent
  participant G as Gemini API
  participant P as Specialist
  participant T as Tools
  participant C as Citation checker
  participant Log as Log (SQLite)

  R->>S: POST /api/decisions/:id/ask {question, audiences, lang}
  Note over R,U: Asked before: the saved run is replayed at US$0. Model unreachable: an offline answer. See seq-offline.
  S->>U: agents loaded, today's spend under the cap,<br/>rate limit ok, a run slot free?
  alt over a limit
    U-->>S: no
    S-->>R: 429 or 503 with a plain message<br/>("the briefs are still here to read")
  else within limits
    U-->>S: yes
    S->>Log: append question.asked (no identity)
    S-->>R: SSE open
    S->>L: run(question, decision)
    L->>G: plan (function calling)
    G-->>L: hand sub-questions to specialists
    L-->>R: SSE plan (steps panel)
    loop each step (at most 40 model calls or US$0.50 per run, each call logs its tokens and cost)
      L->>P: sub-question
      P-->>R: SSE step.start
      P->>G: next action
      G-->>P: call search_pages("bus route 7")
      P->>T: search_pages (BM25 over page text)
      T-->>P: top pages
      P->>T: read_page(source, page)
      T-->>P: page text
      P->>G: page text
      G-->>P: call record_statement(text, citations)
      P->>T: record_statement
      T->>C: is each quote on its page? (normalised match)
      alt every quote found
        C-->>T: verified
        T->>Log: append statement.recorded
        T-->>R: SSE statement (verified)
      else a quote is missing
        C-->>T: rejected, with the reason
        T->>Log: append statement.rejected
        T-->>P: rejected: quote not on page
      end
      P-->>L: verified statements
      P-->>R: SSE step.end
    end
    L->>G: write the answer from the numbered verified statements
    G-->>L: draft answer (code then keeps only cited markers and<br/>drops any sentence with a number no statement backs)
    L->>G: plain-language pass (target grade 8)
    G-->>L: plainer wording
    L->>Log: append answer.given (statements used, calls, cost)
    L-->>R: SSE answer + usage, then done
  end
  Note over R,Log: Each figure is a link that opens the source page with the quote highlighted
